WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.556
CHIATECH JOURNAL explanatory summary: Event Decoration as a Source of Household Income Sustainability in Garkawa, Plateau State, Nigeria: A Descriptive Survey

00:00:10.556 --> 00:00:26.444
Article focus: Background: Event decoration is an increasingly visible creative-service microenterprise in Nigeria and can diversify household livelihoods through income generated from weddings, birthdays, corporate functions, religious events and other ceremonies.

00:00:26.444 --> 00:00:39.667
Research context: Purpose: This study examined the demographic profile, service portfolio, income contribution and operating constraints of practising event decorators in Garkawa, Plateau State, Nigeria.

00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:49.778
Study approach: Methods: A descriptive cross-sectional survey was conducted among 50 practising event decorators using a structured questionnaire.

00:00:49.778 --> 00:00:56.778
Reported findings: Data were analysed with frequencies, percentages and arithmetic means.

00:00:56.778 --> 00:01:09.111
Interpretation: Results: Seventy-six percent of respondents were aged 20–40 years, 56% were women, 56% had secondary education and 24% had tertiary education.

00:01:09.111 --> 00:01:18.333
Publication record: e002 · Volume 1, Issue 1 · July 2026 Pioneer Issue. DOI pending registration.
